==============================================================================
The per-stage reduced system
==============================================================================
n_u = 3, n_c = 2  ->  null space of c_u has dimension 1
free direction (normalised on P_B):  ΔP_Subs = -1.000, ΔP_B = +1.000, Δs = -1.000
  i.e. the ONLY freedom left at a stage is to move power between the
  substation and the battery, with the energy slack following.
residual ‖c_u d‖ = 2.22e-16

With f_uu = c_uu = 0, the stage Hessian is
  Ĥ = diag(0, 2 C_B Δt, 0) + diag(Σ_L + Σ_U) + f_u' V_BB f_u + reg·I
so the reduced Hessian along the single free direction is the SCALAR
  dᵀĤd = (Σ_L+Σ_U)_Psub + 2 C_B Δt + Δt² V_BB + (Σ_L+Σ_U)_P_B
         + Δt² (Σ_L+Σ_U)_s ,        Σ_L = z_l/(u-l),  Σ_U = z_u/(u_hi-u)

The 'dense n_u x n_u KKT solve' is therefore a 1x1 division here, and
the Cholesky that can fail is a positivity test on that one number.
